        <div class="projects-grid stagger-children">
            <!-- PAM -->
            <div class="project-card animate-on-scroll">
                <span class="project-category">Fintech · Payroll Infrastructure · SaaS</span>
                <h3 class="project-name">Payroll Aggregation by M-Works™ (PAM)</h3>
                <p class="project-description">
                    A multi-tenant payroll orchestration platform designed to streamline payroll execution, 
                    statutory obligations, payment initiation and reconciliation for businesses.
                </p>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span>ASP.NET Core 9</span>
                    <span>C#</span>
                    <span>React</span>
                    <span>TypeScript</span>
                    <span>EF Core</span>
                    <span>PostgreSQL</span>
                    <span>REST APIs</span>
                    <span>Docker</span>
                    <span>CI/CD</span>
                </div>
                <button class="case-study-toggle" data-target="pam-detail" aria-expanded="false">
                    View Case Study <span class="arrow">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div class="case-study-detail" id="pam-detail">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <h4>Business Problem</h4>
                        <p>Payroll processing in many South African businesses remains fragmented — statutory calculations, payment initiation and reconciliation are often handled across disconnected systems, leading to errors and delays.</p>
                        <h4>Engineering Challenges</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Designing a multi-tenant architecture with secure tenant isolation.</li>
                            <li>Implementing payroll processing workflows with statutory compliance rules.</li>
                            <li>Building payment integrations for initiating and reconciling payroll disbursements.</li>
                            <li>Ensuring secure API design with authentication and authorisation.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <h4>Architecture & Implementation</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Multi-tenant SaaS with tenant-scoped data access and configuration.</li>
                            <li>ASP.NET Core 9 backend with Entity Framework Core and PostgreSQL.</li>
                            <li>React/TypeScript frontend for payroll management and reporting.</li>
                            <li>Containerised deployments using Docker with CI/CD pipeline automation.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <h4>Key Outcomes</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Functional payroll orchestration with statutory payment workflows.</li>
                            <li>Secure REST API layer supporting multi-tenant operations.</li>
                            <li>Automated deployment infrastructure for rapid iteration.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic;">
                            PAM is a product developed under M-Works™ by Fakade Innovations (Pty) Ltd.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Tshapisa -->
            <div class="project-card animate-on-scroll">
                <span class="project-category">Business Operations · Multi-Tenant SaaS</span>
                <h3 class="project-name">Tshapisa</h3>
                <p class="project-description">
                    A white-label business platform designed to help businesses manage online sales, services, 
                    customer interactions and operational workflows through configurable merchant storefronts.
                </p>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span>ASP.NET Core</span>
                    <span>C#</span>
                    <span>PostgreSQL</span>
                    <span>REST APIs</span>
                    <span>Docker</span>
                </div>
                <button class="case-study-toggle" data-target="tshapisa-detail" aria-expanded="false">
                    View Case Study <span class="arrow">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div class="case-study-detail" id="tshapisa-detail">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <h4>Business Problem</h4>
                        <p>Small and medium businesses often lack affordable, integrated platforms for managing online presence, orders, bookings and logistics from a single system.</p>
                        <h4>Engineering Challenges</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Designing multi-tenant platform architecture with white-label capability.</li>
                            <li>Building configurable product/service catalogues per merchant.</li>
                            <li>Integrating payment gateways and third-party logistics providers.</li>
                            <li>Supporting online ordering, booking workflows and customer interactions.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <h4>Architecture & Implementation</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Multi-tenant architecture with merchant-specific configuration and branding.</li>
                            <li>White-label storefronts with customisable themes and layouts.</li>
                            <li>Payment gateway integrations for secure transaction processing.</li>
                            <li>Third-party logistics integration for order fulfilment.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic;">
                            Tshapisa is a product being developed under M-Works™ by Fakade Innovations (Pty) Ltd.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Retailer Money Transfer -->
            <div class="project-card animate-on-scroll">
                <span class="project-category">Enterprise Fintech · Payments</span>
                <h3 class="project-name">Retailer Money Transfer Platform</h3>
                <p class="project-description">
                    A mission-critical payment platform supporting national retail partners with money transfers, 
                    transaction processing, reconciliation and remediation — processing over 1 million transactions monthly.
                </p>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span>C# / .NET</span>
                    <span>ASP.NET Core</span>
                    <span>SQL Server</span>
                    <span>Entity Framework</span>
                    <span>IIS</span>
                    <span>Azure DevOps</span>
                </div>
                <button class="case-study-toggle" data-target="rmt-detail" aria-expanded="false">
                    View Case Study <span class="arrow">▾</span>
                </button>
                <div class="case-study-detail" id="rmt-detail">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <h4>Business Problem</h4>
                        <p>National retail partners required a robust, high-availability payment platform for money transfer services, with real-time processing, reconciliation and remediation capabilities.</p>
                        <h4>Engineering Challenges</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Ensuring 99.9% availability for a mission-critical financial system.</li>
                            <li>Scaling to handle over 1 million monthly transactions reliably.</li>
                            <li>Implementing enterprise integrations with multiple banking systems and retail partners.</li>
                            <li>Performance optimisation under high-concurrency conditions.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <h4>Architecture & Implementation</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Secure payment processing with end-to-end encryption.</li>
                            <li>Enterprise integrations with internal banking systems and external retail APIs.</li>
                            <li>Hosted on IIS with load balancing, SSL and disaster recovery.</li>
                            <li>Monitored via Grafana and New Relic for real-time observability.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <h4>Key Outcomes</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>99.9% platform availability maintained consistently.</li>
                            <li>More than 1 million monthly transactions processed reliably.</li>
                            <li>Improved performance and deployment automation over time.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic;">
                            This platform was developed during my time at Absa Bank Limited. No proprietary architecture or confidential details are disclosed.
                        </p>
